#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:7
msgid "Untrusted Device Encryption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:10
msgid "Threat Model / Primary Goals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:12
msgid ""
"An \"untrusted\" device can participate in a Syncthing cluster with the "
"following assumptions and limitations;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:15
msgid "The untrusted device can *not* observe:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:17
msgid "File data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:19
msgid "File or directory names, symlink names, symlink targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:21
msgid ""
"File modification time, permissions, or modification history (version "
"vectors)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:24
msgid "The untrusted device *will* be able to observe:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:26
msgid "File sizes [#sizes]_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:28
msgid "Which parts of files are changed by the other devices and when"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:30
msgid ""
"The last point is required by the syncing mechanism, in order to avoid "
"transferring all unchanged file data when a file block changes. Blocks and "
"block hashes are encrypted with a per-file key and depends on the block "
"offset, so correlation is not possible between blocks at different offsets "
"or different files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:36
msgid ""
"In addition the untrusted device *must not* be able to modify, remove or "
"introduce data by itself without detection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:40
msgid "Primitives Used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:42
msgid ""
"The user input to the system is the *folder ID*, which is a short string "
"identifying a given folder between devices, and the *password*. From this we "
"generate a *folder key* (32 bytes) using ``scrypt``::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:46
msgid "folderKey = scrypt.Key(password, \"syncthing\" + folderID)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:48
msgid ""
"The string \"syncthing\" with the folder ID concatenated make up the salt. "
"The folder key is used to encrypt file names using AES-SIV without nonce::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:51
msgid "encryptedFilename = AES-SIV(filename, folderKey)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:53
msgid ""
"Given the key length of 32 bytes the algorithm in use will be AES-128 (\"AES-"
"SIV-256\"). To make the encrypted file name usable again as a file name, we "
"encode it using base32 and add slashes at strategic places."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:57
msgid ""
"From the folder key and the plaintext file name we derive the *file key* by "
"HKDF of the folder key and the plaintext file name::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:60
msgid ""
"fileKey = HKDF(SHA256, folderKey+filename, salt: \"syncthing\", info: nil)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:62
msgid ""
"This file key is used for all other encryption, specifically file block "
"hashes and data blocks. In file metadata, block hashes are encrypted using "
"AES-SIV with the file key::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:66
msgid "encryptedBlockHash = AES-SIV(blockHash, fileKey)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:68
msgid ""
"Data blocks are encrypted using XChaCha20-Poly1305 with random nonces and "
"appended to the nonce itself::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:71
msgid "encryptedBlock = nonce + XChaCha20-Poly1305.Seal(block, nonce, fileKey)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:73
msgid ""
"The original file metadata descriptor is encrypted in the same manner and "
"attached to the encrypted-file metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:76
msgid ""
"Devices sharing a folder need to use the same password. To ensure that a "
"*password token* in the form of an arbitrary, but commonly known string "
"encrypted using AES-SIV with the folder key is sent in the :ref:`cluster-"
"config`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:81
msgid "passwordToken = AES-SIV(\"syncthing\" + folderID, folderKey)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:83
msgid ""
"Thus an encrypted device can verify all its connected devices use the same "
"password comparing the encrypted token, without knowing the password itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:88
msgid ""
"In Syncthing a file is made up of a number of equal size data blocks, "
"followed by a usually shorter last data block. The full size data blocks are "
"at minimum 128 KiB, ranging up to 16 MiB in multiples of two. The last data "
"block can in principle be as small as one byte. For untrusted folders the "
"size of the last data block is padded up to a kilobyte if it was shorter to "
"begin with. The untrusted device isn't allowed to request less than a "
"kilobyte of data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:96
msgid ""
"I don't actually know if this block padding serves a purpose. It was added "
"to address a worry that something might break or leak if an attacker is "
"allowed to repeatedly request single-byte data blocks of their choosing. If "
"there is nothing to worry about here we can remove the padding. //jb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:104
msgid ""
"While a well behaved implementation is expected to request data blocks "
"precisely as announced in the file metadata there is no enforcement of this. "
"This means that an attacker on the untrusted side can repeatedly request "
"arbitrary ranges of a file and receive the encrypted result. With the "
"restriction above, the minimum block size that can be requested in 1024 "
"bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:113
msgid "Implementation Details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:116
msgid "Metadata Encryption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:118
msgid "The Syncthing protocol is essentially two-phase:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:120
msgid ""
"A device sends file metadata (a ``FileInfo`` structure) for a new or changed "
"file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:122
msgid ""
"The other side determines which blocks it needs to construct the new file, "
"and requests these blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:124
msgid ""
"For untrusted devices a fake FileInfo is constructed, with an encrypted name "
"and block list and other metadata such as modification time and permissions "
"set to static values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:128
msgid "An original file metadata structure looks something like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:147
msgid "The fake FileInfo encrypts and adjusts a couple of attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:149
msgid ""
"The name is encrypted (with the folder key), base32 encoded, and slashes are "
"inserted after the first and third characters, and then every 200 characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:153
msgid ""
"The file size is adjusted for the per block overhead, and rounded up so that "
"the last block is a multiple of 1024 bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:156
msgid "The block size is adjusted for block overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:158
msgid ""
"Other file attributes are set to static values, for example the modification "
"time is set to UNIX epoch time 1234567890 and permissions are set to 0644."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:161
msgid "The block list is encrypted and adjusted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:163
msgid "The offset and size are adjusted to account for block overhead"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:165
msgid "The hash is encrypted using AES-SIV (with the file key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:167
msgid ""
"The resulting encrypted hash can't be used for data verification by the "
"untrusted device, but it can be used as a form of \"token\" referring to a "
"given data block for reuse purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:171
msgid ""
"Finally, the whole original FileInfo (in protobuf form) is encrypted using "
"XChaCha20-Poly1305 with the file key and attached to the fake FileInfo. This "
"is retained on the untrusted side and passed along to trusted devices, where "
"it will be used in place of the fake FileInfo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:194
msgid "Incoming Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:196
msgid ""
"File metadata sent from the untrusted device is always decrypted. This means "
"the original FileInfo is discarded and the attached encrypted FileInfo is "
"decrypted and used instead. If the FileInfo does not decrypt it's considered "
"a protocol error and the connection is dropped. This means only file "
"metadata created by a trusted device is accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:203
msgid "Data Encryption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:205
msgid ""
"When an untrusted device makes a request for a data block, the trusted "
"device:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:208
msgid "decrypts the given filename,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:209
msgid "reads the corresponding plaintext data block,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:210
msgid ""
"pads the block with random data if the read returned less than 1024 bytes,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:211
msgid "encrypts it using the file encryption key and a random nonce, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:212
msgid "responds with the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:231
msgid ""
"This is repeated for all required blocks. At the end, the untrusted device "
"appends the fake FileInfo (which includes the original, encrypted, FileInfo) "
"to the file. This serves no purpose during normal operations, but enables "
"offline decryption of an encrypted folder without database access and, in "
"principle, scanning an encrypted folder to populate the database should it "
"be lost or corrupted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:257
msgid "Incoming Data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:259
msgid ""
"Making a request to an untrusted device is mostly the reverse of the above. "
"The file name is encrypted and the block offset and size adjusted. The "
"resulting data is decrypted and thereby also authenticated, meaning it must "
"have originated on a trusted device. Contrary to the usual case we cannot "
"simply make arbitrary range requests -- only the precise blocks that were "
"encrypted to begin with will decrypt properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:266
msgid "---"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/untrusted.rst:268
msgid ""
"Although files grow slightly due to block overhead, and some files are "
"padded up to an even kilobyte, file sizes can be determined at least to the "
"closest kilobyte."
msgstr ""
